    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0538" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">759.6214/62: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Colonel E. M. House </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-30T15:00:00-05:00"
                            >November 30, 1918—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Department has received following telegram from Copenhagen: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“3186, November 24, 2 p.m. My 3155, 18th.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d393-f1"/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Politiken</hi> reported yesterday that
                            Hanssen-Nørremølle arrived Berlin last Friday, and handed to Danish
                            Minister statement to be sent Danish Government wherein Danish
                            population North Schleswig ask Denmark to accept Danish portion of that
                            province. Government are further requested to take up North-Schleswig
                            question at Peace Conference. Grant-Smith.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d393-f1" n="1" xml:id="d393-f1-content">
                <p>See Department’s telegram No. 55, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
